retal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zabner</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>J.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Karp</surname><given-names>P.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Widdicombe</surname><given-names>J.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Welsh</surname><given-names>M.J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Loss of CFTR chloride channels alters salt absorption by cystic fibrosis airway epithelia in vitro</article-title><source>Mol. Cell.</source><volume>2</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>397</fpage><lpage>403</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9774978</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Zeltwangeretal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zeltwanger</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>G.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillis</surname><given-names>K.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hwang</surname><given-names>T.C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gating of cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator chloride channels by adenosine triphosphate hydrolysis. Quantitative analysis of a cyclic gating scheme</article-title><source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source><volume>113</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>541</fpage><lpage>554</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10102935</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Antimicrobial Activity</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr valign="bottom" align="center"><th>Apical solution</th><th>In vitro</th><th>Low salt (washed with H<sub>2</sub>O)</th><th>High salt (washed with 150 mM NaCl)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr valign="bottom"><td align="left">Normal cells</td><td align="center">+++</t